That exact content breaks a lint rule, so this change can't land as written. Its first line imports from `~/cdp/hog-transformations/hog-transformer.service`. The repo rule "ingestion never reaches cdp" (in `nodejs/src/ingestion/Ingestion.spec.md`) says code under `src/ingestion/` must not import `~/cdp`. The `oxlint` `no-restricted-imports` check flags that line, which also works against the aim of this change.

The repo already has the shared contract this file needs, in `src/common/hog-transformations/hog-transformer.interface.ts` (`HogTransformer` and `HogTransformationResult`). A version that passes the lint would be:

```ts
import { HogTransformationResult, HogTransformer } from '~/common/hog-transformations/hog-transformer.interface'
import { PluginEvent } from '~/plugin-scaffold'

export async function transformEventStep(
    event: PluginEvent,
    hogTransformer: HogTransformer | null
): Promise<HogTransformationResult> {
    if (!hogTransformer) {
        return { event, invocationResults: [] }
    }
    return await hogTransformer.transformEventAndProduceMessages(event)
}
```

The logic is the same; only the types come from `~/common` instead of `~/cdp`. I haven't typechecked it, and callers that expect the CDP `TransformationResult` type may need small updates.

Should I switch the file to this version? The other way is to keep your version and ask a person to formally retire the rule. I didn't start that, because the rule still looks correct.

